; Variables declared among the statements (objfpc): scopes, the types of
; values, owned ones.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/inlinevar/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:18:5: error: a variable can only be declared in a statement sequence (between 'begin' and 'end')
; CHECK: errors.pas:20:7: error: redefinition of 'x'
; CHECK: errors.pas:19:7: note: previous definition is here
; CHECK: errors.pas:25:3: error: use of undeclared identifier 'inner'; did you mean 'insert'?
; CHECK: errors.pas:26:16: error: use of undeclared identifier 'self1'
; CHECK: errors.pas:27:12: error: cannot tell the type of 'n' from nil; give the variable a type
; CHECK: errors.pas:28:12: error: cannot tell the type of 'e' from an empty set; give the variable a type
; CHECK: errors.pas:29:18: error: assigning to 'integer' from incompatible type 'string of length 4'
; CHECK: errors.pas:31:5: error: assigning to 'real' from incompatible type 'string of length 2'
; CHECK: errors.pas:32:11: error: 'for' loop control variable must be of an ordinal type, not 'real'
; CHECK: errors.pas:34:3: error: use of undeclared identifier 'j'; did you mean 'e'?
; CHECK: errors.pas:35:16: error: 'for ... in' cannot enumerate a value of type 'integer' (an array, string, set, ordinal type, or an object or record with a GetEnumerator method)
; CHECK: errors.pas:36:11: error: cannot tell the type of 'm' from an empty set; give the variable a type
; CHECK: errors.pas:37:22: error: assigning to 'boolean' from incompatible type 'integer'
; CHECK: errors.pas:43:7: error: owned variable 'q' must be of a class type, not 'integer'
; CHECK: errors.pas:45:3: error: owned variable 'p' was moved
; CHECK: errors.pas:44:8: note: moved here
; CHECK: errors.pas:55:13: error: the object of owned variable 'tmp' can only be stored with 'move tmp'
; CHECK: errors.pas:57:5: error: owned variable 'tmp' was moved
; CHECK: errors.pas:56:13: note: moved here
; CHECK: errors.pas:64:3: error: owned variable 'g' was moved
; CHECK: errors.pas:63:8: note: moved here
; CHECK-NOT: error:
;
; A type or a value is needed; only one variable can have a value.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/inlinevar/syntax.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SYNTAX %s
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:3:12: error: only one variable can be initialized
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:4:14: error: expected ':' and a type, or ':=' and a value, after variable name
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:5:7: error: expected variable name
; SYNTAX-NOT: error:
;
; Only with --mode=objfpc.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=tp -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/inlinevar/tp.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=TP %s
; TP: tp.pas:5:3: error: variables declared among the statements need --mode=objfpc
; TP: tp.pas:6:7: error: expected control variable after 'for'
;
; The tree shows the declaration with its variables and value, and a loop's variable
; before the name that uses it.
; RUN: %p3 --mode=objfpc --emit-ast -o - %S/../run/inlinevar.pas | FileCheck --check-prefix=AST %s
; AST:      VarDeclStmt <50:3>
; AST-NEXT:   VarDecl 'i' : integer <50:7>
; AST-NEXT:   IntegerLiteralExpr 42 : integer <50:12>
; AST:      VarDeclStmt <51:3>
; AST-NEXT:   VarDecl 'big' : int64 <51:7>
; AST:      VarDecl 's' : ansistring
; AST:      ForStmt to <15{{[0-9]}}:3>
; AST-NEXT:   VarDecl 'i' : integer
; AST-NEXT:   NameRefExpr 'i' variable : integer
; AST:      ForInStmt
; AST-NEXT:   VarDecl 's' : ansistring
; AST:      VarDecl 'a' : TNode owned
